---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { brand } from "../brand.js";
---

<Layout
  title="Download Doclira PDF - Windows PDF Toolkit"
  description="Download the free Lite edition of Doclira PDF or purchase the full Windows PDF toolkit."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="guide-page">
    <section class="guide-intro">
      <p class="kicker">DOWNLOAD</p>
      <h1>Start with the free Lite edition.</h1>
      <p>Try the basic Doclira workflow first. When you need commercial use, larger allowances and advanced batch tools, upgrade to a paid plan.</p>
      <div class="actions page-actions">
        <a class="primary" href={brand.liteUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Download free Lite</a>
        <a class="secondary" href="/buy/">Compare paid plans</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-grid">
      <article>
        <p class="step-number">01</p>
        <h2>Download Lite</h2>
        <p>Open the public Lite repository and download the available Windows build or source package.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="step-number">02</p>
        <h2>Install on Windows</h2>
        <p>Doclira is designed for Windows 10 / 11 64-bit. Keep the installer and test with non-sensitive files first.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="step-number">03</p>
        <h2>Try common tasks</h2>
        <p>Preview PDFs, test basic workflows and confirm the app fits your daily document handling.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="step-number">04</p>
        <h2>Upgrade if needed</h2>
        <p>Paid plans unlock the commercial workflow, advanced batch processing and higher AI allowance.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="download-panel">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">WHICH VERSION SHOULD I USE?</p>
        <h2>Lite is for evaluation. Paid plans are for real work.</h2>
        <p>Use Lite to inspect the basic experience. Choose a paid plan when you want a license key, broader batch workflow, AI credits and commercial usage.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="download-cards">
        <article>
          <h3>Free Lite</h3>
          <p>Best for trying the interface and basic workflow.</p>
          <a class="secondary inline-button" href={brand.liteUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open Lite download</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Paid edition</h3>
          <p>Best for recurring office PDF work, AI assistance and commercial use.</p>
          <a class="primary inline-button" href="/buy/">View paid plans</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
